b0 v\\u1eady t\\u00f4i c\\u00f3 th\\u1ec3 tr\\u1ea3 l\\u1eddi \\u0111i\\u1ec1u \\u0111\\u00f3 trong video ti\\u1ebfp theo, v\\u00e0 n\\u1ebfu b\\u1ea1n th\\u1ea5y th\\u00edch"}, {"index": 201, "start": 869.44, "end": 872.44, "text": "video c\\u1ee7a t\\u00f4i, v\\u00ec v\\u1eady h\\u00e3y nh\\u1ea5n n\\u00fat th\\u00edch v\\u00e0 \\u0111\\u0103ng k\\u00fd k\\u00eanh \\u0111\\u1ec3 nh\\u1eadn th\\u00f4ng b\\u00e1o v\\u1ec1"}, {"index": 202, "start": 872.44, "end": 876.0, "text": "c\\u00e1c video. C\\u1ea3m \\u01a1n m\\u1ecdi ng\\u01b0\\u1eddi r\\u1ea5t nhi\\u1ec1u, t\\u1ea1m bi\\u1ec7t!"}], "segments_by_language": {"en": [{"index": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 9.28, "text": "Welcome back Aliens, my name is Devan Reddy and let's continue with this series of Python."}, {"index": 1, "start": 9.28, "end": 13.34, "text": "Now we have talked about what is Python and we have talked about how to install Python"}, {"index": 2, "start": 13.34, "end": 17.52, "text": "on your machine. It's time to start with the actual stuff right and we are waiting for"}, {"index": 3, "start": 17.52, "end": 22.48, "text": "this. Now the step one would be of course you need to open your IDE. Now if you remember"}, {"index": 4, "start": 22.48, "end": 27.08, "text": "in the installation we have installed two softwares. One is the interpreter and second"}, {"index": 5, "start": 27.08, "end": 32.2, "text": "is your PyCharm. But we'll not be using PyCharm in this tutorial. We'll start with"}, {"index": 6, "start": 32.2, "end": 37.32, "text": "the basics so that you will be having that hands-on experience on IDE as well."}, {"index": 7, "start": 37.32, "end": 43.88, "text": "So let's try it out. So what I will do is I will open my IDE and in that so"}, {"index": 8, "start": 43.88, "end": 46.8, "text": "this is your prompt. Okay so this is your prompt. This is where you will type your"}, {"index": 9, "start": 46.8, "end": 51.24, "text": "code now. You know before going for the actual code we have a question here. Why"}, {"index": 10, "start": 51.24, "end": 55.0, "text": "do we code and why do we write a code? Now think about this. We are living in"}, {"index": 11, "start": 55.0, "end": 58.44, "text": "a world where everything is done with the help of computers right. Example if you"}, {"index": 12, "start": 58.44, "end": 63.0, "text": "want to send an SMS, if you want to send an email you don't have to do that. Your"}, {"index": 13, "start": 63.0, "end": 66.72, "text": "computer will do it for you if you instruct it. Example nowadays we have"}, {"index": 14, "start": 66.72, "end": 71.0, "text": "this amazing thing you know we have Siri on iPhone and then we have Google"}, {"index": 15, "start": 71.0, "end": 75.0, "text": "Assistant on Android phones. You know you can ask them to do things for you."}, {"index": 16, "start": 75.0, "end": 78.88, "text": "Example you want to set an alarm you can you know they will do it for you."}, {"index": 17, "start": 78.88, "end": 82.84, "text": "But then how they understand what you want to say. So you need to talk to a"}, {"index": 18, "start": 82.84, "end": 86.64, "text": "computer and if you want to talk to a computer you need to understand their"}, {"index": 19, "start": 86.64, "end": 90.64, "text": "language right and the language which computer understands is binary code"}, {"index": 20, "start": 90.64, "end": 94.68, "text": "which is zeros and ones. Now that means if you want to talk to computer you need"}, {"index": 21, "start": 94.68, "end": 98.4, "text": "to you need to talk to them in terms of zeros and ones. Now it is not"}, {"index": 22, "start": 98.4, "end": 101.44, "text": "practically possible right of course. So what you have to do is you need to"}, {"index": 23, "start": 101.44, "end": 106.36, "text": "use a language which will which both will understand and of course do we so"}, {"index": 24, "start": 106.36, "end": 110.72, "text": "we all know English language but computer will not understand plain English"}, {"index": 25, "start": 110.72, "end": 115.28, "text": "right because we have some grammatical stuff here. So what we have done is we"}, {"index": 26, "start": 115.28, "end": 120.12, "text": "have created programming languages now those are not actually example we have"}, {"index": 27, "start": 120.12, "end": 124.76, "text": "high-level languages now those are not exactly a binary code and they're not"}, {"index": 28, "start": 124.76, "end": 129.76, "text": "even exactly same as English. They are somewhat you know they have their"}, {"index": 29, "start": 129.76, "end": 133.36, "text": "own protocols they have their own grammar which we use. So when I say"}, {"index": 30, "start": 133.36, "end": 136.92, "text": "English so we have level one English then we have level two which is"}, {"index": 31, "start": 136.92, "end": 140.2, "text": "programming language and then we have level three which is your which is"}, {"index": 32, "start": 140.2, "end": 143.52, "text": "your binary format. So you understand English so what you will do is you will"}, {"index": 33, "start": 143.52, "end": 147.92, "text": "learn a programming language let's say Python in this case and then you will"}, {"index": 34, "start": 147.92, "end": 151.2, "text": "write a Python code which will get converted into a binary format which"}, {"index": 35, "start": 151.2, "end": 154.92, "text": "a computer will understand. So if you say hey computer do something for me so"}, {"index": 36, "start": 154.92, "end": 158.8, "text": "let's go with this very simple stuff here let's I want to add two numbers. So you"}, {"index": 37, "start": 158.8, "end": 162.56, "text": "will say hey computer 2 plus 3 a computer will say okay 5 but then how"}, {"index": 38, "start": 162.56, "end": 165.92, "text": "you talk to a computer in this case. So we are using Python and then we have"}, {"index": 39, "start": 165.92, "end": 170.08, "text": "an interpreter in fact in Python it's one of as we discussed it's one of the"}, {"index": 40, "start": 170.08, "end": 174.0, "text": "easiest language right. So what I will do is I will say 2 plus 3 this is the"}, {"index": 41, "start": 174.0, "end": 178.48, "text": "simplest task you can do on Python so I will say 2 plus 3 it works you can see"}, {"index": 42, "start": 178.48, "end": 182.72, "text": "we got 5 yeah so this is working what else what about subtraction you know we"}, {"index": 43, "start": 182.72, "end": 186.72, "text": "love mathematics right so let's apply all the arithmetic operations here. Let's"}, {"index": 44, "start": 186.72, "end": 192.64, "text": "try 9 minus 8 it should be 1 and we got 1 so yes subtraction also works okay"}, {"index": 45, "start": 192.64, "end": 197.56, "text": "what else we can use can we use multiplication let's try 4 into 6 it should"}, {"index": 46, "start": 197.56, "end": 201.96, "text": "be 24 yeah that's right we got the answer so yes addition subtraction"}, {"index": 47, "start": 201.96, "end": 205.64, "text": "multiplication works what about division okay let's try so when I say division it"}, {"index": 48, "start": 205.64, "end": 212.0, "text": "should be 8 divided by 4 and I'm expecting answer to be 2 yeah it's 2 but"}, {"index": 49, "start": 212.0, "end": 215.92, "text": "hold on there is a difference here you can see if when we say 2 plus 3 we got"}, {"index": 50, "start": 215.92, "end": 221.28, "text": "5 9 minus 8 which is 1 so when you subtract two numbers we are getting"}, {"index": 51, "start": 221.28, "end": 225.0, "text": "that number right and specifically this are integer numbers right we all use"}, {"index": 52, "start": 225.0, "end": 229.92, "text": "integers but then when you divide a number it is giving you a point value now"}, {"index": 53, "start": 229.92, "end": 233.76, "text": "this point which is also called as float numbers so we have integers and then we"}, {"index": 54, "start": 233.76, "end": 240.2, "text": "have float now float stands for floating point representation okay but why it is"}, {"index": 55, "start": 240.2, "end": 245.08, "text": "2.0 because when you divide numbers you might get point values right example"}, {"index": 56, "start": 245.08, "end": 249.56, "text": "when you say 5 divided by 2 you will get 2.5 example let's try it out so if I"}, {"index": 57, "start": 249.56, "end": 254.24, "text": "say 5 divided by 2 you got 2.5 and you want that point 5 value right that's why"}, {"index": 58, "start": 254.24, "end": 259.24, "text": "it converts your number or your output into a float value because you want it"}, {"index": 59, "start": 259.24, "end": 263.36, "text": "they want to give you the exact value but what if you don't want it what if you"}, {"index": 60, "start": 263.36, "end": 268.48, "text": "want only the quotient part example when I say 5 divided by 2 you want only 2 you"}, {"index": 61, "start": 268.48, "end": 272.2, "text": "don't want point point 5 value so we can do that you know we if you want"}, {"index": 62, "start": 272.2, "end": 276.72, "text": "only integer output so we don't want float now we want only integer you"}, {"index": 63, "start": 276.72, "end": 280.44, "text": "can do that you can say 5 instead of giving 1 slash you have to give 2 slash"}, {"index": 64, "start": 280.44, "end": 284.2, "text": "now this is also called as integer division or it is also called as flow"}, {"index": 65, "start": 284.2, "end": 289.12, "text": "division so when I say run this code you got 2 so this is working yeah okay what"}, {"index": 66, "start": 289.12, "end": 292.64, "text": "else we can do here can I do you know combination of this arithmetic"}, {"index": 67, "start": 292.64, "end": 299.24, "text": "operational example let's say 8 plus 9 yeah and then subtracted by let's say"}, {"index": 68, "start": 299.24, "end": 302.96, "text": "10 is it possible and let's try it so it works you know so you can have"}, {"index": 69, "start": 302.96, "end": 308.12, "text": "multiple operations but then we have to follow grammar right if you say 8 plus 9"}, {"index": 70, "start": 308.12, "end": 312.52, "text": "and then subtract you forgot to type 10 there it will give you an error which is"}, {"index": 71, "start": 312.52, "end": 317.12, "text": "invalid syntax and that's why you need to follow the grammar as well so in as in"}, {"index": 72, "start": 317.12, "end": 320.48, "text": "when you learn a language you need to follow grammars in the same way in"}, {"index": 73, "start": 320.48, "end": 323.92, "text": "programming as well you have to follow grammar can I use those bracket stuff"}, {"index": 74, "start": 323.92, "end": 327.92, "text": "which we used to use in mathematics yes we can for example let's say we have"}, {"index": 75, "start": 328.08, "end": 334.04, "text": "8 and then I am adding that value but then I also have a value which is 2 into 3 now"}, {"index": 76, "start": 334.04, "end": 337.84, "text": "which one will be done first of course the multiplication part right but then"}, {"index": 77, "start": 337.84, "end": 341.4, "text": "what if you want to do it or let's try this first so you can see we got 14"}, {"index": 78, "start": 341.4, "end": 346.96, "text": "which is 8 plus 6 but what if I want to say 8 plus 2 which is 10 and then 3 so"}, {"index": 79, "start": 346.96, "end": 351.04, "text": "in that case you need to use brackets right if remember the board mass rule so"}, {"index": 80, "start": 351.04, "end": 355.36, "text": "I will say 8 plus 2 which is in the brackets and then into 3 so you can"}, {"index": 81, "start": 355.36, "end": 358.96, "text": "see we got 30 so yes this also works so when you multiply so if you give a"}, {"index": 82, "start": 358.96, "end": 362.96, "text": "bracket it will be solved first okay this is cool right now what else we can do"}, {"index": 83, "start": 362.96, "end": 367.68, "text": "here what if I want to find a power of or you can say exponent you know so let's"}, {"index": 84, "start": 367.68, "end": 372.88, "text": "say if you have