ave done with that right, we are saying two plus three."}, {"index": 8, "start": 32.8, "end": 36.64, "text": "Now if you remember in max what we do is we of course we work with numbers but then"}, {"index": 9, "start": 36.64, "end": 42.72, "text": "when the moment you start with algebra you have this concept of using x and y so"}, {"index": 10, "start": 42.72, "end": 46.68, "text": "what we do is we say let x is equal to five can you do that here?"}, {"index": 11, "start": 46.68, "end": 52.56, "text": "So we have x equal to two so I'm storing this value two in a variable called as x"}, {"index": 12, "start": 52.56, "end": 55.36, "text": "and that's a new word now what is variable?"}, {"index": 13, "start": 55.36, "end": 59.64, "text": "So basically variable is a container where you can put your values example we"}, {"index": 14, "start": 59.64, "end": 64.92, "text": "are storing two here in a container and the name of that container is x of course"}, {"index": 15, "start": 64.92, "end": 69.32, "text": "you can give any name doesn't matter you can say abc you can say a box you can"}, {"index": 16, "start": 69.32, "end": 73.6, "text": "give any name right so we can say x equal to two and the moment I say enter now"}, {"index": 17, "start": 73.6, "end": 77.44, "text": "this is the first time when you said enter and you have not got any output"}, {"index": 18, "start": 77.44, "end": 81.72, "text": "right so in the earlier from what we did is when we said any any operation it"}, {"index": 19, "start": 81.72, "end": 86.16, "text": "was giving you some output here we have not got any output it's it's just an"}, {"index": 20, "start": 86.16, "end": 90.8, "text": "assignment operation so in assignment what we do is we have a variable name equal"}, {"index": 21, "start": 90.8, "end": 96.28, "text": "to a value so we are assigning two to x okay that works so can I you cannot do"}, {"index": 22, "start": 96.28, "end": 100.88, "text": "this now can I say x plus three yes right because in x we have a value which is two"}, {"index": 23, "start": 100.88, "end": 105.88, "text": "or it works you can see we got five that works can I store three as well let's"}, {"index": 24, "start": 105.88, "end": 111.24, "text": "try so I will say y is equal to three now we have two variables x and y so we"}, {"index": 25, "start": 111.24, "end": 117.72, "text": "have two boxes and now I will say x plus y oh it works right it works so we can say"}, {"index": 26, "start": 117.72, "end": 123.28, "text": "x has to y has three and we are adding them okay so that's why we can we can"}, {"index": 27, "start": 123.28, "end": 127.56, "text": "use them but then why they are called as variables now normally when you say"}, {"index": 28, "start": 127.56, "end": 131.6, "text": "variable this term simply means you can change the value can we change here"}, {"index": 29, "start": 131.6, "end": 136.96, "text": "can I say x equal to 9 can I change the value from 2 to 9 let's try and the"}, {"index": 30, "start": 137.08, "end": 142.8, "text": "say enter oh it works there there was no error but now if I try to do this if I"}, {"index": 31, "start": 142.8, "end": 150.08, "text": "say x plus y x will have a value which is 2 or 9 that's a question because we are"}, {"index": 32, "start": 150.08, "end": 155.68, "text": "changing it but there's no error enter oh you got 12 that means the value of x"}, {"index": 33, "start": 155.68, "end": 159.96, "text": "now is 9 okay so we can change the value and now we can justify that what"}, {"index": 34, "start": 159.96, "end": 163.92, "text": "as variables right so what is variable it's a box where you can have a value"}, {"index": 35, "start": 164.24, "end": 169.28, "text": "now do we need to define the type of the variable you don't need to so the moment I assign a value"}, {"index": 36, "start": 169.28, "end": 174.32, "text": "you can it automatically detects what type of value you are assigning so in this case it is integer"}, {"index": 37, "start": 174.32, "end": 179.76, "text": "now let's do this thing what if I say x and if I say enter what it will do so the moment you say"}, {"index": 38, "start": 179.76, "end": 185.92, "text": "x and enter it will print the value of x in this case which is 9 right what if I use a variable"}, {"index": 39, "start": 185.92, "end": 190.32, "text": "abc now of course we have not defined this variable right and we are still trying to use it"}, {"index": 40, "start": 190.4, "end": 197.44, "text": "the moment I say enter you got an error the error is it says name error abc name abc is not defined"}, {"index": 41, "start": 197.44, "end": 202.72, "text": "and that's why we have not defined abc yet so if you are if you are using a variable which is not"}, {"index": 42, "start": 202.72, "end": 207.36, "text": "defined so it will of course give you an error now I will do one more thing I will say x plus 10"}, {"index": 43, "start": 207.36, "end": 213.28, "text": "so of course it will give you 19 now what if I want to add 19 with y I mean something this"}, {"index": 44, "start": 213.28, "end": 218.08, "text": "something in this way I would say 19 plus y but then if you think about this 19 this is the"}, {"index": 45, "start": 218.08, "end": 223.44, "text": "output of the previous operation right now if you want to use the output of the previous operation"}, {"index": 46, "start": 223.44, "end": 228.56, "text": "we can use underscore so underscore represents the output of the previous operation and if I say"}, {"index": 47, "start": 228.56, "end": 234.16, "text": "enter you can see we got 22 so it is 19 plus 3 which is 22 so even this works right so this is"}, {"index": 48, "start": 234.16, "end": 238.56, "text": "amazing you know there are so many things you can you can work with this so we can use variables"}, {"index": 49, "start": 238.56, "end": 244.72, "text": "for for numbers right so we can use it for float or integer what about string can I use names with"}, {"index": 50, "start": 244.72, "end": 249.92, "text": "can I use variables with string or the string variable let's try so I will get a variable as name"}, {"index": 51, "start": 250.48, "end": 257.76, "text": "and I will use a name as youtube and if I say enter oh it works and if I print name we got youtube so"}, {"index": 52, "start": 257.76, "end": 265.28, "text": "it is perfectly working so we can use string as well so example I can say name plus youtube rocks"}, {"index": 53, "start": 265.28, "end": 269.76, "text": "so you can you can see we got youtube rocks so it is name which is youtube plus rocks okay this"}, {"index": 54, "start": 269.84, "end": 274.4, "text": "even this work that's perfectly fine in fact let me just do an experiment can I say name"}, {"index": 55, "start": 274.96, "end": 280.32, "text": "and space rocks okay this is not working so we have to make sure that you put plus there because"}, {"index": 56, "start": 280.32, "end": 285.12, "text": "if you have plus then then only it will try to interpret that but there's this one thing which"}, {"index": 57, "start": 285.12, "end": 289.6, "text": "is very fancy here you know so we'll talk about youtube it's a string right and it's a combination"}, {"index": 58, "start": 289.6, "end": 295.12, "text": "of characters that means even if I want to fetch one character it should be able we should be"}, {"index": 59, "start": 295.12, "end": 300.4, "text": "able to do that right and yes we can do that so if I say name and if I want to fetch one character"}, {"index": 60, "start": 300.4, "end": 305.04, "text": "how will I do that so let's say if I have a youtube here and youtube has seven letters or seven"}, {"index": 61, "start": 305.04, "end": 309.44, "text": "characters if you when you break it down it will create an array or you can say collection of"}, {"index": 62, "start": 309.44, "end": 314.0, "text": "characters the numbering starts with zero because normally in computers numbering always starts"}, {"inde