, "start": 389.6, "end": 393.68, "text": "reverse order now now what if I want to print two characters not one two so let's say I want to"}, {"index": 77, "start": 393.68, "end": 399.92, "text": "print y and o so in this case I will say name and I will start with zero of course we want to"}, {"index": 78, "start": 399.92, "end": 404.32, "text": "print zero the first character and the second character right that means we will give two"}, {"index": 79, "start": 404.32, "end": 408.88, "text": "but this two doesn't mean number of characters it means the ending so I want to start with zero"}, {"index": 80, "start": 408.88, "end": 415.36, "text": "and one so first two characters and you can see we got y zero the same thing if I do it for one"}, {"index": 81, "start": 415.36, "end": 421.52, "text": "colon four so come on guess so one means second character right so it will start with o and it"}, {"index": 82, "start": 421.52, "end": 428.64, "text": "will end at three because you cannot include four so it will it is exclusive of four so it is"}, {"index": 83, "start": 428.72, "end": 437.92, "text": "one which is o u and t oh it works we got out yeah so yeah so out it works now what if I specify"}, {"index": 84, "start": 437.92, "end": 443.2, "text": "only one and colon if I don't specify the ending what happens in this case it will start with one"}, {"index": 85, "start": 443.2, "end": 447.92, "text": "and it will come it will go till the end okay that house works so if you don't specify the ending"}, {"index": 86, "start": 447.92, "end": 452.8, "text": "part it will go in that way what if I specify the ending part but not the starting point example if I"}, {"index": 87, "start": 452.8, "end": 458.88, "text": "say or if I if I keep it blank and after colon I will say four now in this case it will start with"}, {"index": 88, "start": 458.88, "end": 464.72, "text": "the first letter and it will end at three which is before four and that's why you got y o u t so this"}, {"index": 89, "start": 464.72, "end": 470.88, "text": "fun right okay what else we can do here what if I specify name and I will give wrong values I will"}, {"index": 90, "start": 470.88, "end": 476.8, "text": "say three colon ten of course we don't have ten characters right now in this case it will end"}, {"index": 91, "start": 476.8, "end": 481.2, "text": "at the last one which is available so it will not give you any other in this at this case you"}, {"index": 92, "start": 481.2, "end": 487.12, "text": "can see we got t u b e tube start with t and then it's end at e because we don't have any other"}, {"index": 93, "start": 487.12, "end": 491.6, "text": "characters so if you don't if you want to avoid errors this is what this is one way okay now can"}, {"index": 94, "start": 491.6, "end": 499.44, "text": "I change the letter example I don't want it to be youtube I want to I want it to be my tube so"}, {"index": 95, "start": 499.44, "end": 508.4, "text": "I will say name from zero to three I want to change this with my can I do that so I'm changing"}, {"index": 96, "start": 508.4, "end": 514.96, "text": "y o u to my the moment I say enter you got an error it says string object does not support item"}, {"index": 97, "start": 514.96, "end": 519.68, "text": "assignment so the thing is once you assign the value you cannot change it not even for one"}, {"index": 98, "start": 519.68, "end": 525.04, "text": "character if I say zero I want to change the first character to rot you even this will not"}, {"index": 99, "start": 525.04, "end": 529.36, "text": "work you can see we got the error so you cannot change the value that means strings in python"}, {"index": 100, "start": 529.36, "end": 534.96, "text": "is immutable you cannot change the value of it that's awesome right but then that doesn't"}, {"index": 101, "start": 535.04, "end": 539.84, "text": "means you cannot you cannot change while printing example if I if I want to print my tube you can"}, {"index": 102, "start": 539.